# trixie-backports gives us the newer kernel (7.1, matching VyOS's closer
# behaviour and picking up in-kernel OpenVPN DCO/ovpn) and a newer Kea
# (3.0.3 vs. trixie's 2.6.3) without pulling the rest of backports in.
#
# `lb config --backports true` (see build-vyos-image) already adds an
# equivalent entry derived from --mirror-chroot at build time; this static
# file is kept in addition so the trixie-backports.pref.chroot pin below
# has a source it clearly corresponds to even if that flag's behaviour
# changes. A duplicate apt source for the same repository is harmless.
deb http://deb.debian.org/debian trixie-backports main contrib non-free non-free-firmware
